# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BrowserForWP — ignore rules
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Visual Studio / MSBuild build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.binlog
*.tlog
*.log

# Visual Studio user state (never share these)
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.userprefs
.vs/

# WP / WinRT package output
AppPackages/
BundleArtifacts/
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.appxupload
*.xap
*.xapupload
*.pfx
*.cer

# NuGet
packages/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# Test / coverage
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage/
*.coverage
*.trx

# Node (build tooling only — see tools/)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Python (asset generator only — see tools/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Generated build artifacts we DO want to keep are committed explicitly;
# everything below is generated on demand:
#   tools/gen-vectors.mjs  -> tools/out/*.json  (tracked, see docs)

# Visual Studio running in the Windows guest, over the shared folder. It resolves
# its user state relative to the folder it is started from, so `devenv` run
# inside the repo leaves an empty `Visual Studio 2013/Backup Files/<solution>/`
# directory per solution it opened, plus a copy of its ItemTemplates and
# ProjectTemplates under `Visual Studio 2013Templates/`. Neither is source, both
# are written as root (deleting them needs sudo), and a measuring run creates
# them without asking -- see docs/MAINTAINING.md "Troubleshooting".
Visual Studio 2013*/

# Agent tooling. The skills themselves ARE committed under .agents/skills/,
# with skills-lock.json pinning source and hash so `npx skills experimental_install`
# can restore them. What is not source: .claude/skills/, a directory of relative
# symlinks into .agents/skills/ that `npx skills add` regenerates per agent.
.claude/

# Scratch workspace for plan execution (subagent-driven-development /
# executing-plans): per-plan ledgers, task briefs, review packages. Its own
# .gitignore also covers it; this line means a fresh clone without that file
# still ignores it.
.superpowers/
